{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nNormal compaction (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:522-654`), rebuild (`compact_rebuild.py:107-238`), and recovery (`compact_recovery.py:128-202`) compute the same things with different code: candidate listing (`compact_txn.py:196-223` vs `compact_rebuild.py:59-84` vs `compact.py:176-225`), which uuids are sources (`compact_txn.py:633-637` filter added after bug `privileged-nephelite-colt`; rebuild skipped snapshots from day one at `compact_rebuild.py:76-79`), the snapshot envelope (`compact_txn.py:297-326` vs inline `compact_rebuild.py:164-195`, docstring admits \"mirroring\"), the retire/rollback rule (`compact_txn.py:329-454`, `compact_recovery.py:128-164`; the rebuild retire loop at `compact_rebuild.py:198-205` has no rollback — bug `compulsory-pernickety-mantis`), the two-arm \"needs folding\" rule (`compact.py:228-283` vs `compact_trigger.py:118-147`), and the commit step (`compact_txn.py:401-415`, `compact_rebuild.py:88-103`, `compact.py:314-350`). Open story `plush-excessive-willet` (snapshot as derived cache) is a design change that this planner makes cheaper; it does not overlap.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `src/rebar/_commands/compact_plan.py`: `list_candidates(ticket_dir) -> list[Candidate]`, `needs_folding(candidates, threshold, horizon, now)`, `source_uuids_of(candidates)` (the SNAPSHOT-exclusion rule in one place), `build_snapshot_event(...)`, `retire_or_rollback(...)` / `restore_retired(...)`, `commit_ticket_dir(git, ticket_id, message)`. The three paths consume it; rebuild gains rollback for free. Crash-safety mechanisms (intent journal, `.bak`, in-process abort) are unchanged — fsck remains the sole owner of mixed state per `compact_recovery.py:22-26`. Guard: the `*.retired` rename-back rule and the snapshot envelope builder exist once.\n\n\n## Guard construction\nFollow the guard-test construction rule in the parent epic `airborne-wellloved-kingfisher`: owner module exempt, match the constituent conjunction or AST shape named in Approach (or the definition count where no distinctive atom exists), `# <construct>-ok: <reason>` escape marker, and behaviour pinned only by the named existing tests.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_commands/compact_plan.py` (new), `compact_txn.py`, `compact_rebuild.py`, `compact_recovery.py`, `compact.py`, `compact_trigger.py`, `tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py` (new). `_compact_locked` and `compact_all_cli` sit at their C901 ceilings, so edits there are subtractive only.\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: normal and rebuild over the same ticket directory produce snapshot events with identical `source_event_uuids`. Edge: rebuild interrupted after the first rename rolls back. Pinning: `tests/unit/test_compact_crash_atomicity.py`, `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_process_death.py` (real SIGKILL at the rename barrier), `tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py`, `tests/unit/test_creation_channel_compaction.py`, `tests/unit/test_compact_rebuild_counter_b2bb.py` (`_REBUILD_COUNT` stays in `compact_rebuild`) pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Normal and rebuild agree on `source_event_uuids` for every fixture ticket; checked by the new equivalence test.\n- [ ] A rebuild killed between two renames leaves the ticket directory restorable and fsck-clean; checked by a SIGKILL test at the existing barrier env var.\n- [ ] Pinning suites pass unchanged and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports no `increased`; checked by running both.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787355002586861001,"uuid":"a71e22f8-16d4-424c-b9cb-bc705c88ff96"}